From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Hughes <ryan@heyoodle.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:10:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] HID: multitouch: mark the ProArt N1x PixArt touchpads as
 pressure pads

The PixArt 093A:4F01 and 093A:4F02 haptic touchpads on the ASUS ProArt
P16 H7607BA and P14 H7407BA report each contact's force in Tip
Pressure, in grams, without a Button Type feature saying they are
pressure pads. libinput reads the axis as contact size and starts a
touch only above about 10% of its range, so light touches, or on the
P14 every touch, did nothing until a libinput quirk set
INPUT_PROP_PRESSUREPAD.

Set the property for these two touchpads.
---
 drivers/hid/hid-multitouch.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/hid/hid-multitouch.c b/drivers/hid/hid-multitouch.c
index 4e19a0c4d..71d425f62 100644
--- a/drivers/hid/hid-multitouch.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-multitouch.c
@@ -2114,6 +2114,18 @@ static void mt_expired_timeout(struct timer_list *t)
 	clear_bit_unlock(MT_IO_FLAGS_RUNNING, &td->mt_io_flags);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Touchpads that report each contact's force in Tip Pressure, without the
+ * Button Type feature that would say so. Reading that axis as contact size,
+ * libinput needs a press of over 10% of its range to start a touch.
+ */
+static const struct hid_device_id mt_pressurepad_ids[] = {
+	/* PixArt haptic touchpads on the ASUS ProArt P16 and P14 (NVIDIA N1x) */
+	{ HID_I2C_DEVICE(USB_VENDOR_ID_PIXART, 0x4f01) },
+	{ HID_I2C_DEVICE(USB_VENDOR_ID_PIXART, 0x4f02) },
+	{ }
+};
+
 static int mt_probe(struct hid_device *hdev, const struct hid_device_id *id)
 {
 	int ret, i;
@@ -2140,6 +2152,7 @@ static int mt_probe(struct hid_device *hdev, const struct hid_device_id *id)
 	td->hdev = hdev;
 	td->mtclass = *mtclass;
 	td->inputmode_value = MT_INPUTMODE_TOUCHSCREEN;
+	td->is_pressurepad = hid_match_id(hdev, mt_pressurepad_ids);
 	hid_set_drvdata(hdev, td);
 
 	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&td->applications);
